>  First I sample theta0 from the beta(1,13)

This is not right. Stan does not sample like JAGS or BUGS.

theta0~beta(1,13)

The snippet above does not assign a value to theta0 but it increments the log probability ('target'). I think you will have to follow the advice from the other post you found. Have a look at chapter 27 in the Stan Reference Manual. It explains the difference between assigning a value to a parameter and incrementing the log probability better than I can.

