I'd recommend switching to a Cholesky factor parameterization
of correlation matrices and use our LKJ prior with an independent
prior on the scales.  It's what we recommend in the manual and it's
a lot faster and more arithmetically stable when paired with
multi_normal_cholesky.  We haven't gotten around to writing the
(inverse) Wishart on the Cholesky factor parameterization.

- Bob

